surprising to do that

257
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:39,616
after I've buzzed you
into the building.

258
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:41,618
So, Phoebe...

259
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:44,287
why are there men's shoes
by the door?

260
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:46,498
Those are my shoes.

261
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:49,959
Oh. Well, when you get over this
breakup, we need to go shopping.

262
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:52,212
Look, Monica,

263
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:54,464
I really appreciate
you checking in on me,

264
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:56,508
but I'm actually feeling
a lot better.

265
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:57,884
Really?
Yeah.

266
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,718
I just kind of want
to be alone right now.

267
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,720
( knock on door )

268
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:03,306
Who's that?

269
00:12:03,348 --> 00:12:05,433
I ordered Chinese food.

270
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:11,981
What are the chances?!

271
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:15,902
One billion Chinese people,
and they send Mike!

272
00:12:20,407 --> 00:12:23,076
What are you
doing here?
Phoebe called me.

273
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,743
Phoebe!

274
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:26,496
I'm sorry, I broke down.

275
00:12:26,538 --> 00:12:27,955
I wanted to see him.

276
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,541
Damn it, Phoebe,
how did you even call him?

277
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:32,001
There's a speaker phone
on the base unit.

278
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:33,127
Base unit!

279
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,589
Think, Monica, think!

280
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,798
Look, if I want to see Phoebe,
and she wants to see me--

281
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,509
This doesn't concern you.

282
00:12:39,551 --> 00:12:43,930
Sorry. I guess I was thrown off
by the mention of my name.

283
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:47,141
Look, guys, you
can't do this.

284
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:48,727
It's just going
to make getting

285
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:50,478
over each other
that much harder.

286
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:52,146
Not if nothing happens.

287
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:54,773
Why can't... why can't we
just hang out as friends?

288
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,817
Sure.

289
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,737
If you're just going
to hang out as friends,

290
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,154
then, then maybe
I'll join you.

291
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,948
Yeah, I'm your friend
and Mike's friend.

292
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,491
Yeah.

293
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:07,537
Sit down.

294
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:11,916
MONICA:
Oh, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.

295
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:14,377
Make room for your friend.

296
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:16,087
There you go. Ah.

297
00:13:23,637 --> 00:13:24,929
So how have you been?

298
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:27,890
I've been
pretty good.

299
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:33,146
You look really
beautiful.

300
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,147
Thanks.

301
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,273
You look good, too.

302
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:36,857
No, no, no,
no, no, no.

303
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:38,859
This is dangerous territory.

304
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,111
Keep it clean.

305
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,615
So how's the
piano playing going?

306
00:13:43,657 --> 00:13:45,366
Actually, I've
been playing

307
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:47,160
a lot of love
songs lately.

308
00:13:47,201 --> 00:13:48,244
I've missed you.

309
00:13:48,286 --> 00:13:51,247
I've missed you, too.

310
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:55,042
You know, on the way
over here,

311
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:59,838
I saw this drunk guy
throw up...

312
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,258
and then
a pigeon ate it.

313
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,515
Hey. Ross.

314
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:11,726
Look, I just wanted
to apologize for...

315
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:14,061
Don't tell me
you actually made

316
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:16,022
those gay pictures of me.

317
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,231
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

318
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,441
Check this out.

319
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:19,858
Huh.

320
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:22,403
So, that's what I'd look
like if I worked out...

321
00:14:22,445 --> 00:14:26,073
and was being serviced
by a policeman.

322
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:28,535
You're not going to actually
send these out, are you?

323
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:30,244
Uh, actually, no,
I don't need to

324
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:33,373
because your little "Ross is
dead" joke didn't work, okay?

325
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,666
There were no responses.

326
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:36,668
Nobody posted anything
on the Web site.

327
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,044
Nobody called my parents.

328
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,838
So, the joke,
my friend, is on you.

329
00:14:39,878 --> 00:14:41,756
Nobody called,
nobody wrote anything.

330
00:14:41,798 --> 00:14:43,257
Nobody cares that I'm dead.

331
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:50,223
Oh, my God.

332
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:52,475
Nobody cares
that I'm dead?

333
00:14:52,517 --> 00:14:54,728
Oh, come on, you know
that's not true.

334
00:14:54,769 --> 00:14:56,312
What are you
talking about?

335
00:14:56,354 --> 00:14:59,440
You get 60 responses just for
coming out of the closet.

336
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:02,151
I didn't get one response,
and-and I'm dead.

337
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:03,528
Well, the gay community

338
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:06,155
is a lot more vocal
than the dead community.

339
00:15:06,197 --> 00:15:07,532
I can't believe this.

340
00:15:07,574 --> 00:15:10,451
Not even my geology lab partner?

341
00:15:10,493 --> 00:15:12,620
And I carried that guy!

342
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,581
All right, look, let's
think about this, okay?

343
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:16,457
Do you really think
that people are going to

344
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:18,209
disturb your family
at this tragic time?

345
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:21,212
That people are going to post
condolences on a Web site?

346
00:15:21,254 --> 00:15:24,006
This isn't about people
not caring that you're dead.

347
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:27,343
This about people not having a
decent outlet for their grief.

348
00:15:27,385 --> 00:15:29,763
You're right,
there isn't a decent outlet.

349
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:31,389
Right, I mean,
come on.

350
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:33,349
I'm sure if you had a funeral
or memorial service,

351
00:15:33,391 --> 00:15:34,684
tons of people would come.

352
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,978
Exactly!

353
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,272
Ross, what are you,

354
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:41,399
what are you,
what are you doing?

355
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:43,610
You're having a memorial
service for yourself?

356
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:44,611
What?

357
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,696
No. That would be stupid.

358
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:48,155
You're having it for me.

359
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,616
Ross, don't press that.

360
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:50,825
Don't press that!

361
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,410
Too late, too late.
It's sent.

362
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:56,456
Oops, sorry, so's that picture
of you and the policeman.

363
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,334
I'm trying to put
Emma down for a nap.

364
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:01,836
Have you seen Huggsy?

365
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:03,922
Uh, original or crappy?

366
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:06,215
Original.

367
00:16:06,257 --> 00:16:07,842
No, sorry, haven't seen him.

368
00:16:07,884 --> 00:16:10,052
Then what's that big lump
under your covers?

369
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:13,890
It's Monica, okay?

370
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,182
That is not Monica.

371
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:16,225
All right, fine!

372
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,978
It's original Huggsy.

373
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,483
I know Emma wants him,
but he's mine, and I need him.

374
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,944
She's being unreasonable.

375
00:16:25,984 --> 00:16:27,236
Joey, there is a reason that

376
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:28,696
Emma loves that stupid penguin
so much!

377
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:29,656
( gasps )

378
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:30,949
Oh, don't cover its ears!

379
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:36,370
It's because it reminds her
of her Uncle Joey.

380
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,538
It does?

381
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,874
Yeah, and she's
comforted

382
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:43,962
by him because she loves
her Uncle Joey so much.

383
00:16:44,002 --> 00:16:45,797
Really? She, she loves me?

384
00:16:45,839 --> 00:16:48,007
Oh, yeah.

385
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,133
But you know what?

386
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:51,218
If you need Huggsy, don't worry.

387
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,095
Emma will totally understand.

388
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:54,764
I won't, but whatever.

389
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:57,391
Okay, wait, wait, w-wait, wait
a minute, wait a minute, Rach.

390
00:16:57,433 --> 00:17:02,605
I mean if, if... if Huggsy
means that much to Emma, then...

391
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:04,858
Well, she can have him.

392
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:07,986
Aw... oh, sweet, I knew
Uncle Joey would step up.

393
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,737
Look, Emma, look
who's back...

394
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:12,156
No, forget it,
forget it, I can't do it.

395
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:14,032
Are you kid-- you're
going to take Huggsy

396
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:15,409
away from a little child?

397
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,871
How do you think I got him
in the first place?

398
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:21,499
All right, you two,

399
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:22,959
I'm going to go
to the bathroom.

400
00:17:23,001 --> 00:17:25,003
Now, I don't want anything
going on while I'm gone.

401
00:17:25,043 --> 00:17:27,254
All right, here's a few things
you can discuss:

402
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:31,676
Mucus, fungus, and the idea
of me and Ross doing it.

403
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,639
I've missed
you so much.

404
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:38,850
No, I'm not going to ask
you to get back together

405
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:40,685
because I know we want
different things,

406
00:17:40,727 --> 00:17:42,353
but just to be with
you one more night.

407
00:17:42,395 --> 00:17:43,688
I know,
I want that too,

408
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:45,857
but is that going
to make it too hard?

409
00:17:45,899 --> 00:17:47,775
It can't be any
harder than this.

410
00:17:47,817 --> 00:17:50,611
I mean, if I had known
the last time I saw you

411
00:17:50,653 --> 00:17:52,321
would be the last time I...

412
00:17:52,363 --> 00:17:54,991
I would have stopped
to memorize your face,

413
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:57,493
the way you move...
everything about you.

414
00:17:57,535 --> 00:18:00,038
If I had known the
last time I kissed you

415
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,622
would be the last time...

416
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:03,833
I never would have stopped.

417
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:07,545
Kiss him, you fool!

418
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:09,797
What?

419
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:11,632
Didn't you hear that speech?

420
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:13,885
If you don't kiss him,
then I will.

421
00:18:13,927 --> 00:18:15,929
I've missed you so much.

422
00:18:17,263 --> 00:18:19,640
I knew you'd be here!

423
00:18:19,682 --> 00:18:20,850
Aah, crap.

424
00:18:20,892 --> 00:18:23,061
Who, who is this?

425
00:18:23,101 --> 00:18:25,229
It's my friend Manny.

426
00:18:25,271 --> 00:18:28,608
I asked him to keep
me away from you.

427
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,944
Hey, that's what
I'm doing for Phoebe.

428
00:18:30,985 --> 00:18:33,613
Well, you're not doing
a very good job.

429
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:35,073
Excuse me?

430
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,323
What's with the kissing?

431
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:38,576
Hey, at least I knew
where my guy was.

432
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:40,870
Oh, yeah, yeah, thank
God you were here

433
00:18:40,912 --> 00:18:42,455
to oversee
all the kissing!

434
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:45,083
You didn't hear the speech.

435
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,125
I've heard the speech.

436
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,501
If he knew it was going to be

437
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:48,878
the last time he saw her...

438
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,046
Hey, it was
very moving.

439
00:18:50,088 --> 00:18:51,047
You're just heartless.

440
00:18:51,089 --> 00:18:51,798
You're weak.

441
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,591
You're... weird.

442
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:55,134
Your pants are undone.

443
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:56,260
Oh!

444
00:18:58,763 --> 00:18:59,931
Where'd they go?

445
00:19:00,932 --> 00:19:03,309
Oh. Damn it!

446
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:04,518
Oh, we blew it.

447
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,897
I blame myself.

448
00:19:07,939 --> 00:19:10,357
And I blame you, too.

449
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,282
It's been an hour,
and not one

450
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:20,451
of my classmates
has shown up?

451
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:22,120
I tell you, when I actually die,

452
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,622
some people are going
to get seriously haunted.

453
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:26,874
( knock on door )

454
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:27,917
There you go.

455
00:19:27,959 --> 00:19:29,293
Someone came.

456
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:31,295
Okay, okay, I'm,
I'm going to go hide.

457
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:33,923
Oh, this is so exciting,
my first mourner.

458
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:38,970
Hi.

459
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,680
Glad you could come.

460
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:41,973
Please come in.

461
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:43,099
Hi.

462
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:44,600
You're Chandler Bing, right?

463
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:45,768
I'm Tom Gordon.

464
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:46,936
I was in your class.

465
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:48,688
Oh, yes, yes.
Let me take your coat.

466
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,148
Thanks.

467
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:53,275
Uh, I'm, I'm so sorry
about Ross. It's...

468
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,695
Well, at least he died
doing what he loved.

469
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:57,071
Watching blimps.

470
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,453
Who is it?

471
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:05,955
I don't know--
some guy, Tom Gordon.

472
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:07,498
I don't remember him.

473
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:10,501
But, then again,
I touched so many lives.

474
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:15,631
So did you
know Ross well?

475
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:17,133
Oh, actually,
I barely knew him.

476
00:20:17,175 --> 00:20:19,177
Yeah, I came because
I heard Chandler's news.

477
00:20:19,217 --> 00:20:20,678
You know if he's
seeing anyone?

478
00:20:24,974 --> 00:20:27,143
Yes, he is. Me.

479
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:28,895
What? ( stuttering )

480
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:32,481
Oh. Oh, can I ask you
a personal question?

481
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:36,069
How, how do you shave
your beard so close?

482
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:40,614
Okay, Tommy, that's
enough mourning for you.

483
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:41,615
Here we go.

484
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:42,533
Bye-bye.

485
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,284
All right.
All right.

486
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:45,870
Hey, listen... call me.

487
00:20:45,912 --> 00:20:47,245
Okay.

488
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:52,752
I'm dead and
no one cares?

489
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:55,629
I look like a man?

490
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:58,465
Please, one ridiculous
problem at a time.

491
00:20:58,507 --> 00:20:59,967
This isn't
ridiculous.

492
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:01,719
Look around. No one's here.

493
00:21:01,761 --> 00:21:03,221
You gave them
one day's notice.

494
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,471
Not everyone
in our class

495
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:05,890
checks the Web site
every day,

496
00:21:05,932 --> 00:21:08,142
and Monica, it's probably
the way you stand.

497
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:11,520
All right.

498
00:21:11,562 --> 00:21:13,522
Still, somebody
must have seen it.

499
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:16,192
I mean, I went to that school
for four years

500
00:21:16,234 --> 00:21:18,444
and I didn't have
an impact on anyone?

501
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:19,779
Well, that's
not true.

502
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,321
You had
an impact on me.

503
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,032
I mean it's
15 years later

504
00:21:23,074 --> 00:21:24,951
and we're still
best friends.

505
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,953
Doesn't that count
for something?

506
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,287
Man.

507
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:30,998
( knock on door )

508
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:34,627
Oh, great, more party
boys for Chandler.

509
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,294
I'm sure it's
somebody for you.

510
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:37,546
Now go hide.

511
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:43,510
Hi.

512
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,930
I'm here for Ross Geller's
memorial service.

513
00:21:45,972 --> 00:21:47,431
Kori?

514
00:21:47,473 --> 00:21:49,183
Kori Weston?

515
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,309
Yeah.

516
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:52,394
You look amazing.

517
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:53,562
And you are?

518
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:55,273
Chandler. Chandler Bing.

519
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:57,608
I'm not gay,
I'm not gay at all.

520
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,277
You are
married,
though.

521
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:00,444
Don't listen to him.

522
00:22:00,486 --> 00:22:01,988
He's in a
really bad mood.

523
00:22:05,992 --> 00:22:07,409
I can't believe

524
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:08,661
that Ross is gone.

525
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,037
It is just so sad.

526
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:12,206
Oh, I didn't know
Ross and you were so close.

527
00:22:12,248 --> 00:22:15,293
Oh, we weren't,
but we had one class together.

528
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:16,961
He was such a great guy,

529
00:22:17,003 --> 00:22:19,964
and he talked so passionately
about science.

530
00:22:20,006 --> 00:22:21,715
I always remembered him.

531
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:23,926
I'm sure that would
mean a lot to him

532
00:22:23,968 --> 00:22:25,511
and if heaven has a door,

533
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:28,181
I'm sure he's pressing
his ear up against it

534
00:22:28,222 --> 00:22:29,682
and listening intently.

535
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:35,271
I thought so many times about
calling him and asking him out.

536
00:22:35,313 --> 00:22:37,564
I guess I really
missed my chance.

537
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:39,317
No, you didn't!

538
00:22:41,861 --> 00:22:43,821
I'm still alive!

539
00:22:43,863 --> 00:22:45,739
Kori, I, I

540
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:47,616
know this is a big
surprise for you.

541
00:22:47,658 --> 00:22:50,286
It's a long story,
but the things you just said

542
00:22:50,328 --> 00:22:51,954
really made my day.

543
00:22:51,996 --> 00:22:54,372
I mean, the fact that you
are here means more to me

544
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:57,210
than, than if this room
were filled with people.

545
00:22:57,251 --> 00:22:59,461
You sick freak!
Who does that?

546
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:02,215
I can't believe
I had a crush on you!

547
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,303
( door slams )

548
00:23:07,345 --> 00:23:09,263
Did you hear that?

549
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:13,309
Kori Weston had a crush on me.

550
00:23:13,351 --> 00:23:16,770
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

551
00:23:20,733 --> 00:23:23,361
No, Mom, I am not dead.

552
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:28,324
No, I know it's not
something to kid about.

553
00:23:28,366 --> 00:23:31,827
Anyway, it was just a practical
joke between Chandler and me,

554
00:23:31,869 --> 00:23:33,120
but it's over, okay?

555
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:35,331
Actually, no,
even if I had died,

556
00:23:35,373 --> 00:23:39,417
you would not be left childless.

557
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:41,461
Monica?

